#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Writes this case's fixture data into the run's workspace (both arms see the same files).
# Generated by benchmarks/builder; edit the case script there, not this file.
set -euo pipefail
mkdir -p resources
cat > resources/notes.md <<'DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF'
# Notes
- Quillstack sells workflow software to finance teams; annual contracts.
- lead_cohorts_by_source.csv: contacts by creation month and original source, with how many of them have ever entered each lifecycle stage (from the stage entry date properties), as of 30 September 2026. create_method shows form fills vs list imports.
- lifecycle_stage_snapshot.csv: contacts by their current lifecycle stage today.
DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF
cat > resources/demand_gen_review.md <<'DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF'
# Demand generation review, Jan-Sep 2026 (marketing ops)

## Cost per lead by source
| Source | Spend | Leads | Cost per lead |
|---|---|---|---|
| content_syndication | $188,872 | 5,358 | $35 |
| events | $154,900 | 2,216 | $70 |
| linkedin_ads | $277,185 | 2,286 | $121 |
| paid_search | $275,821 | 1,056 | $261 |

## Funnel
- MQL to SQL conversion is only 10% (lifecycle stage report, today): sales is not working our MQLs.
- Webinars have produced 0 customers since launch in August.
- Pipeline created Jan-Sep (sum of opportunity amounts): paid_search $4,968,000, linkedin_ads $1,728,000, content_syndication $855,000, events $2,354,000. LinkedIn Ads creates $6.2 of pipeline per dollar against $18.0 for paid search; we plan to cut it in Q1.
- Win rate 29% (won / (won + lost)); median sales cycle 48 days.

## Recommendation for Q4
Move the paid search budget ($30,647 a month) into content syndication, our cheapest lead source, and stop webinars.
DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF
